Description: Keep an error list, and report end of input in a tag or comment
 The tokenizer and tree states carry an error list, which parse() returns
 as "errors". Each error is a code and the facts about it, such as the
 range read and the start of the tag, with no wording. Each tag state's
 end-of-input step reports "eof-in-tag", and the comment state reports
 "eof-in-comment" with the range of its "<!--". The data state reports
 "eof-in-tag" for a "<", "<!" or incomplete doctype left at the end. The
 tokenizer records where each tag starts for these reports.
Author: Numiko
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Test: test/parser/diagnostics.test.ts ("eof-in-tag", "eof-in-comment"); npm run test:upstream
Last-Update: 2026-11-04
